      "text": " Here, we have:\n- 6 \u00d7 5 = 30, which is 3 in the tens place and 0 in the ones place.\n- 6 \u00d7 4 = 24, which is 2 in the tens place and 4 in the ones place.\n- 7 \u00d7 5 = 35, which is 3 in the tens place and 5 in the ones place.\n- 7 \u00d7 4 = 28, which is 2 in the tens place and 8 in the ones place.\n\n4. Add the numbers in each diagonal, carrying over if necessary:\n```\n  6 | 7\n\u00d7 5 | 4\n-----\n 30 | 28\n 35 | 28\n-----\n 30 | 28\n 35 | 28\n-----\n 30 | 28\n 35 | 28\n-----\n 36 | 18\n```\n5. Read the final product from the bottom and right edges of the grid:\n```\n  36 | 18\n```\n\nTherefore, using the lattice method, we have shown that the product of 67 and 54 is 3618. <|User|>Can you also show me how to solve this using the standard long multiplication method? <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c> <think>\nCertainly! The standard long multiplication method involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number, starting from the rightmost digit, and then adding the results together. Let's go through the steps for multiplying 67 by 54 using the standard long multiplication method.\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nCertainly! To solve the multiplication of 67 and 54 using the standard long multiplication method, we'll follow these steps:\n\n1. Write the numbers one above the other, aligning them by place value:\n```\n   67\n\u00d7  54\n-----\n```\n\n2. Multiply 67 by the ones digit of 54 (which is 4):\n```\n   67\n\u00d7  4\n-----\n  268\n```\n3. Multiply 67 by the tens digit of 54 (which is 5, and remember to shift one place to the left):\n```\n   67\n\u00d7 50\n-----\n 3350\n```\n4. Add the two results together:\n```\n  268\n+3350\n-----\n 3618\n```\n\nTherefore, using the standard long multiplication method, we have shown that the product of 67 and 54 is 3618. <|User|>Can you also show me how to solve this using the standard long multiplication method, but this time starting with the tens digit of 54? <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c> <t