messages:  ['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 100 and 77? Please reason step by step.I think the correct answer is: 7600\n\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 100 and 77, we need to understand what multiplication means. Multiplication is essentially a shortcut for repeated addition. In this case, we are asked to find the product of 100 and 77, which means we need to add 100 to itself 77 times or add 77 to itself 100 times. However, for simplicity, we can use the standard multiplication method.\n</think>\n<answer>\nTo find the product of 100 and 77, we can use the standard multiplication method. We multiply the digits as follows:\n1. Multiply the units digit of 100 (which is 0) by the units digit of 77 (which is 7): \\(0 \\times 7 = 0\\).\n2. Multiply the tens digit of 100 (which is 0) by the units digit of 77 (which is 7): \\(0 \\times 7 = 0\\).\n3. Multiply the hundreds digit of 100 (which is 1) by the units digit of 77 (which is 7): \\(1 \\times 7 = 7\\).\n4. Multiply the units digit of 100 (which is 0) by the tens digit of 77 (which is 7): \\(0 \\times 7 = 0\\).\n5. Multiply the tens digit of 100 (which is 0) by the tens digit of 77 (which is 7): \\(0 \\times 7 = 0\\).\n6. Multiply the hundreds digit of 100 (which is 1) by the tens digit of 77 (which is 7): \\(1 \\times 7 = 7\\).\n7. Multiply the units digit of 100 (which is 0) by the hundreds digit of 77 (which is 7): \\(0 \\times 7 = 0\\).\n8. Multiply the tens digit of 100 (which is 0) by the hundreds digit of 77 (which is 7): \\(0 \\times 7 = 0\\).\n9. Multiply the hundreds digit of 100 (which is 1) by the hundreds digit of 77 (which is 7): \\(1 \\times 7 = 7\\).\n\nNow, we add all these products together:\n\\[0 + 0 + 7 + 0 + 0 + 7 + 0 + 0 + 7 = 21\\]\n\nSince we are dealing with the product of 100 and 77, we need to consider the place value. The number 100 has two zeros, so we need to add two zeros to the end of the sum:\n\\[2100\\]\n']
