      "text": "Now, we need to multiply 62 by 90 (the tens digit of 97, which is 9 with a zero added at the end):\n```\n  62\n\u00d7 90\n-----\n 5580\n```\nTo get this, we can think of it as multiplying 62 by 9 and then adding a zero at the end:\n```\n  62\n\u00d7  9\n-----\n 558\n```\nThen we add this result to the previous one:\n```\n  434\n+5580\n-----\n 6014\n```\nTherefore, the product of 62 and 97 is 6014, not 6114 as you initially thought. The correct answer is 6014.\n</answer>",
