gredients:\n\\[ \\text{Total Cost} = \\$2.00 + \\$2.25 + \\$0.50 + \\$0.30 = \\$5.05 \\]\n\nNext, apply a 10% discount to the total cost:\n\\[ \\text{Discount} = 0.10 \\times \\$5.05 = \\$0.505 \\]\n\nSubtract the discount from the total cost:\n\\[ \\text{Final Cost} = \\$5.05 - \\$0.505 = \\$4.545 \\]\n\nFinally, calculate the total weight, total volume, total surface area, and total energy content of all ingredients:\n- Total Weight: \\(600 \\text{ grams} + 300 \\text{ grams} + 300 \\text{ grams} + 120 \\text{ grams} = 1320 \\text{ grams}\\)\n- Total Volume: \\(100 \\text{ cubic centimeters} \\times 4 + 50 \\text{ cubic centimeters} \\times 3 + 120 \\text{ cubic centimeters} \\times 2 + 100 \\text{ cubic centimeters} \\times 1 = 400 + 150 + 240 + 100 = 990 \\text{ cubic centimeters}\\)\n- Total Surface Area: \\(200 \\text{ square centimeters} \\times 4 + 150 \\text{ square centimeters} \\times 3 + 180 \\text{ square centimeters} \\times 2 + 160 \\text{ square centimeters} \\times 1 = 800 + 450 + 360 + 160 = 1770 \\text{ square centimeters}\\)\n- Total Energy Content: \\(100 \\text{ calories/cup} \\times 4 + 80 \\text{ calories/cup} \\times 3 + 120 \\text{ calories/cup} \\times 2 + 90 \\text{ calories/cup} \\times 1 = 400 + 240 + 240 + 90 = 1070 \\text{ calories}\\)\n\nSo, the final cost of the ingredients for the fruit salad after applying the discount is $4.545, the total weight of the ingredients is 1320 grams, the total volume of the ingredients is 990 cubic centimeters, the total surface area of the ingredients is 1770 square centimeters, and the total energy content of the ingredients is 1070 calories. This method simplifies the calculation by breaking it down into smaller, more manageable multiplications, additions, subtractions, and multiplications, making it easier to compute the final cost, total weight, total volume, total surface area, and total energy content after applying the discount. <|User|>Can you provide an example of how the distributive proper