od is 23115.\n\nHere's the detailed breakdown:\n\n```\n  300 × 60 = 18000\n  300 × 7 = 2100\n  40 × 60 = 2400\n  40 × 7 = 280\n  5 × 60 = 300\n  5 × 7 = 35\n-----------------\n 18000 + 2100 + 2400 + 280 + 300 + 35 = 23115\n```\n\nThe final answer is:\n```\n  23115\n```<|User|>Can you provide an example of how to solve the same problem, 345 × 67, using the lattice method one more time for completeness? <｜Assistant｜> <think>\nCertainly! Let's go through the lattice method one more time to solve the problem of multiplying 345 and 67. The lattice method involves creating a grid and breaking down the multiplication into smaller parts, then summing the diagonals. Here are the steps:\n\n1. **Draw a 3x2 grid**:\n   - The grid will have 3 rows and 2 columns, corresponding to the place values of 345 and 67.\n\n2. **Write the digits along the top and left side of the grid**:\n   ```\n   345\n   67\n   ```\n\n3. **Multiply each digit along the top by each digit along the left side and write the result in the corresponding cell of the grid, splitting the tens and units digits**:\n   ```\n   3 | 4 | 5\n   6 | 7\n   -----\n   18 | 24 | 30\n   21 | 28 | 35\n   ```\n\n4. **Add the numbers in each diagonal of the grid, carrying over if necessary**:\n   - Start with the top left diagonal: 18 + 21 = 39 (write 9 and carry 3)\n   - Next diagonal: 24 + 28 + 3 = 55 (write 5 and carry 5)\n   - Bottom right number: 30 + 35 = 65 (write 65)\n\n5. **Combine the sums**:\n   - 39 (from the top left diagonal) + 55 (from the next diagonal) + 65 (from the bottom right number) = 159\n\nTherefore, the product of 345 and 67 using the lattice method is 23115.\n\nHere's the grid filled in with the calculations:\n\n```\n  3 | 4 | 5\n  6 | 7\n-----\n 18 | 24 | 30\n 21 | 28 | 35\n-----\n 39 | 55 | 65\n-----\n 23115\n```\n\nThe final answer is:\n```\n  23115\n```<|User|>Can you provide an example of how to solve the same problem, 345 × 67, using the area model one more time for completeness? <｜Assistant｜> <t