messages:  ["Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 39 and 91? Please reason step by step.I think the correct answer is: 3546\n\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 39 and 91, we can use the standard multiplication method. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. However, for simplicity, we can also use the distributive property of multiplication over addition to break down the problem into smaller, more manageable parts.\n</think>\n<answer>\nFirst, let's break down the numbers 39 and 91 into their components:\n- 39 can be written as 40 - 1\n- 91 can be written as 90 + 1\n\nNow, we can use the distributive property to multiply:\n\\[ 39 \\times 91 = (40 - 1) \\times (90 + 1) \\]\n\nUsing the distributive property:\n\\[ (40 - 1) \\times (90 + 1) = 40 \\times 90 + 40 \\times 1 - 1 \\times 90 - 1 \\times 1 \\]\n\nNow, let's calculate each term:\n\\[ 40 \\times 90 = 3600 \\]\n\\[ 40 \\times 1 = 40 \\]\n\\[ -1 \\times 90 = -90 \\]\n\\[ -1 \\times 1 = -1 \\]\n\nNow, add these results together:\n\\[ 3600 + 40 - 90 - 1 = 3599 \\]\n"]
