messages:  ["Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 99 and 99? Please reason step by step.I think the correct answer is: 8801\n\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 99 and 99, we can use the standard multiplication method or recognize a pattern that simplifies the calculation. Let's go through both methods.\n</think>\n<answer>\nFirst Method: Standard Multiplication\n1. We can start by writing 99 and 99 one below the other and then multiply each digit of 99 by each digit of 99, just like we do in regular multiplication.\n2. 99 x 99 = (90 + 9) x (90 + 9)\n3. Using the distributive property of multiplication over addition, we can expand this as:\n   (90 x 90) + (90 x 9) + (9 x 90) + (9 x 9)\n4. Calculating each term:\n   90 x 90 = 8100\n   90 x 9 = 810\n   9 x 90 = 810\n   9 x 9 = 81\n5. Adding these results together:\n   8100 + 810 + 810 + 81 = 9791\nSo, the product of 99 and 99 is 9791.\nSecond Method: Recognizing a Pattern\nAnother way to solve this problem is to recognize that 99 is 100 - 1. This allows us to use the difference of squares formula, which states that (a - b)(a + b) = a² - b².\n1. In this case, a = 99 and b = 1.\n2. Applying the formula:\n   (99 - 1)(99 + 1) = 99² - 1²\n3. Calculating the squares:\n   99² = 9801\n   1² = 1\n4. Subtracting the squares:\n   9801 - 1 = 9791\nBoth methods give us the same result, confirming that the product of 99 and 99 is 9791.\n</answer>\n"]
