messages:  ["Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 91 and 98? Please reason step by step.I think the correct answer is: 8912\n\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 91 and 98, we can use the standard multiplication method. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. However, for simplicity, we can also use the distributive property of multiplication over addition, which will make the calculation easier.\n</think>\n<answer>\nFirst, let's break down the numbers 91 and 98 into their components:\n- 91 can be written as 90 + 1\n- 98 can be written as 90 + 8\n\nNow, we can use the distributive property to multiply these numbers:\n\\[ 91 \\times 98 = (90 + 1) \\times (90 + 8) \\]\n\nUsing the distributive property, we expand this expression:\n\\[ (90 + 1) \\times (90 + 8) = 90 \\times 90 + 90 \\times 8 + 1 \\times 90 + 1 \\times 8 \\]\n\nNow, let's calculate each term separately:\n1. \\( 90 \\times 90 = 8100 \\)\n2. \\( 90 \\times 8 = 720 \\)\n3. \\( 1 \\times 90 = 90 \\)\n4. \\( 1 \\times 8 = 8 \\)\n\nNext, we add these results together:\n\\[ 8100 + 720 + 90 + 8 = 8918 \\]\n"]
