messages:  ["Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 23 and 13? Please reason step by step.I think the correct answer is: 269\n\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 23 and 13, we can use the standard multiplication method. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nFirst, let's write the numbers one above the other for clarity:\n```\n  23\n× 13\n```\nWe can break this into two parts: multiplying 23 by 3, and then multiplying 23 by 10 (which is the same as multiplying by 1 and then shifting the result one place to the left).\n1. Multiply 23 by 3:\n```\n  23\n×  3\n-----\n  69\n```\n2. Multiply 23 by 10 (which is the same as multiplying 23 by 1 and then shifting the result one place to the left):\n```\n  23\n× 10\n-----\n 230\n```\n"]
