  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "Now, we need to multiply 96 by 50 (the tens digit of 57, which is 5 times 10):\n```\n  96\n\u00d7 50\n-----\n 4800\n```\nTo get this, we can simply add a zero at the end of 96 because we're multiplying by 50 (which is 5 times 10).\nNext, we add the two results together:\n```\n  672\n+4800\n-----\n 5472\n```\nTherefore, the product of 96 and 57 is 5472, not 5772 as you initially thought.\n</\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\n</answer>",
