messages:  ["Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 62 and 19? Please reason step by step.I think the correct answer is: 1174\n\n<think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 62 and 19, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nFirst, let's write the numbers one above the other for clarity:\n```\n  62\n× 19\n```\nWe can break this into two parts: multiplying 62 by 9, and then multiplying 62 by 10 (which is the same as multiplying by 1 and then shifting the result one place to the left).\n1. Multiply 62 by 9:\n```\n  62\n×  9\n-----\n 558\n```\n2. Multiply 62 by 10 (which is the same as multiplying 62 by 1 and then shifting one place to the left):\n```\n  62\n× 10\n-----\n 620\n```\n"]
