      "text": "Now we have:\n4 \u00d7 180\nTo find 4 \u00d7 180, we can break it down further:\n4 \u00d7 180 = 4 \u00d7 (100 + 80)\n= (4 \u00d7 100) + (4 \u00d7 80)\n= 400 + 320\n= 720\nTherefore, the product of 40 and 18 is 720.\n</answer>",
