      "text": "Now, let's calculate each part separately:\n1. \\( 62 \\times 20 \\):\n   - To multiply 62 by 20, we can think of it as multiplying 62 by 2 and then adding a zero at the end.\n   - \\( 62 \\times 2 = 124 \\)\n   - Adding a zero gives us \\( 1240 \\).\n\n2. \\( 62 \\times 5 \\):\n   - To multiply 62 by 5, we can use the fact that \\( 62 \\times 5 = 62 \\times (10 / 2) \\).\n   - First, calculate \\( 62 \\times 10 = 620 \\).\n   - Then, divide by 2: \\( 620 / 2 = 310 \\).\n\nNow, we add the two results together:\n\\[ 1240 + 310 = 1550 \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 62 and 25 is \\( 1550 \\).\n\nThe correct answer is: 1550.\n</answer>",
