it for each item to determine which item has the highest average cost per unit.\n\n- Item A: $15\n- Item B: $20\n- Item C: $10\n- Item D: $12\n- Item E: $18\n- Item F: $8\n\nThe item with the highest average cost per unit is **Item B** with an average cost per unit of $20.\n\n### Finding the Total Cost of All Items in Both Shopping Carts Combined\nTo find the total cost of all items in both shopping carts combined, we sum the total costs of both shopping carts.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total Cost} = 170 + 104 = 274\n\\]\n\n### Finding the Total Quantity of All Items Combined\nTo find the total quantity of all items combined, we sum the quantities of all items.\n\n- Total quantity of Item A: 4 units\n- Total quantity of Item B: 3 units\n- Total quantity of Item C: 5 units\n- Total quantity of Item D: 3 units\n- Total quantity of Item E: 2 units\n- Total quantity of Item F: 4 units\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total Quantity} = 4 + 3 + 5 + 3 + 2 + 4 = 21\n\\]\n\n### Finding the Average Cost per Unit for All Items Combined\nTo find the average cost per unit for all items combined, we first calculate the total cost of all items and the total quantity of all items.\n\n- Total cost of all items: $274\n- Total quantity of all items: 21\n\nNow, we calculate the average cost per unit for all items combined:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average Cost per Unit for All Items} = \\frac{274}{21} \\approx 13.05\n\\]\n\n### Finding the Average Quantity per Unit for All Items Combined\nTo find the average quantity per unit for all items combined, we divide the total quantity of all items by the total number of items.\n\n- Total number of items: 6\n\n\\[\n\\text{Average Quantity per Unit for All Items} = \\frac{21}{6} = 3.5\n\\]\n\n### Summary of Both Scenarios\n- **First Shopping Cart:**\n  - Total Cost: $170\n  - Average Cost per Unit:\n    - Item A: $15\n    - Item B: $20\n    - Item C: $10\n\n- **Second Shopping Cart:**\n  - Total Cost: $104\n  - Average Cost per Unit:\n    - Item D: $12\n    - Item E: $18\n    - Item