      "text": "Now, we need to multiply 77 by 60 (the tens digit of 66, which is 6 multiplied by 10):\n   77\n   \u00d7 60\n   -----\n   4620\n6. We add these two results together:\n   462\n   +4620\n   -----\n   5082\n7. Therefore, the product of 77 and 66 is 5082.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe correct answer is 5082.\n</answer>",
